    "type": "question",
    "label": "3",
    "prompt": "Any number that is divisible by 18 is also divisible by 3 and 6. The opposite is not always true. Write down a number larger than 100 that is divisible by 3 and 6, but not divisible by 18.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "For example, $114$.",
      "worked": "$114>100$. Its digit sum is $1+1+4=6$, so it is divisible by $3$. It is also even, so it is divisible by $6$.\n\n$18\\times6=108$ and $18\\times7=126$. Since $108<114<126$, it is not divisible by $18$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
